## Contract
ClientServer topology readiness: `framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/06-observability/01-runtime-monitoring.ko.md:194` — `ready` = host serving and the topology can process application messages; ReadyTargetCount includes local and remote Ready Servers with positive weight (dotnet interface :379 wording; the language interface doc for your language is the projection). A **Server-only** ClientServer host (manual peer source, weight > 0, host Serving) must report topology Ready / isReady=true / readyTargetCount=1. A Client-only host with no ready Server is not ready. Outbound Client-role checks (send/request on a Server-only host → NotConfigured) stay with their existing owner. Reference fix: dotnet commit "ClientServer topology readiness counts the local Ready Server" (`ZLinkClientServerRuntimeService.cs`, `ClientServerChannelRuntimeTests.cs:632-693`) and `doc/plan/c016-worklog/fix-dotnet-cs-server-only-ready-summary.md` (parity table).

